    "gitCommitMessage": "Real quiz grading from played notes + single hearts source of truth\n\nQuizzes now grade what the learner actually plays instead of always passing:\n\n- BLE note input: expose subscribeNotes() from the BLE layer. The firmware\n  already streams [0x01, midiNote] key presses (previously used only for\n  calibration); a persistent monitor now feeds them to listeners for the whole\n  connection.\n- Engine grading: a 'quiz' step waits for the learner to play the target\n  note(s). Each expected key turns green as it's played; wrong notes cost a\n  heart and trigger a shake/'oops'. Pure gradeNote() helper (unit-tested) drives\n  correct / repeat (harmless double-press) / wrong decisions. notePlayed() is\n  fed by BOTH on-screen key taps and live BLE presses, so it works with or\n  without the hardware.\n- Single hearts source of truth: the engine starts from the learner's real,\n  persisted hearts (initialHearts) and each wrong note calls onWrongNote ->\n  loseHeart(), removing the old divergent local counter and double-counting.\n- Accurate stars/accuracy: onComplete now reports hearts-left and a real\n  accuracy (correct notes / notes asked) computed in the engine, instead of a\n  lagging ref that always yielded 3 stars.\n- UX: replace the fake 'I played it' button with a green 'Play the highlighted\n  keys' prompt; 'HEAR IT' replays the target. Stabilise engine callbacks via an\n  optsRef so the per-render opts object no longer churns the BLE subscription.\n\nAdds quizGrading.ts + 6 unit tests (29 total pass).",
